        "id": "1-1",
        "num": "1.1",
        "title": "Welcome & Core Values",
        "html": "\n<p>Established by Hamish Doig in 1992, our team specialise in commercial real estate sales and leasing. Our widely experienced team have developed a reputation as being the leading provider of commercial real estate services in the South Island. We also have held the honour of being Colliers International NZ franchise of the year.</p>\n<h4>History of South Island Commercial Limited</h4>\n<p>Hamish Doig is Managing Director of Colliers International in Christchurch. He founded the Christchurch office of Colliers International in 1992, fully purchasing it in 1998. In 2004 the name changed to South Island Commercial (2004) Limited, trading as Colliers International, and in June 2015 it changed to South Island Commercial Limited when Mark Macauley joined the company as a shareholder and General Manager. From an original staff of 4, we have grown to 31.</p>\n<p>In September 2014 Agri Realty Limited joined the Colliers family of businesses. The Agri business works from our Christchurch office, and they also have an office in Ashburton. The shareholders of this company are Shane O'Brien, Ruth Hodges, Greg Anderson and Hamish Doig.</p>\n<h4>Vision</h4>\n<p>To be a highly respected professional services organisation that consistently provides quality solutions to its clients. This will be provided by a committed and motivated team of professionals who will ensure the continual development of a sustainable, quality driven business through their own continual development.</p>\n<h4>Core Values</h4>\n<p>Our <strong>CAN DO</strong> values are at the core of all we do:</p>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>C</strong>reate a client focussed environment</li>\n<li><strong>A</strong>ble to focus, prioritise and achieve satisfaction for clients</li>\n<li><strong>N</strong>urture relationships with clients, listen, collaborate and provide them with efficient service</li>\n<li><strong>D</strong>o be responsible &amp; resilient &amp; do as promised</li>\n<li><strong>O</strong>pen communication, honestly and with a mind open to change, both internally and externally</li>\n</ul>\n<h4>Organisational Culture</h4>\n<p>We want a culture which supports and encourages initiative, creativity, imagination, flexibility, hard work, responsibility and the ability to spot and grasp business opportunities. We want open and honest two-way communications.</p>\n<p>Teamwork, collaboration and cooperation are rewarded through the team enjoying greater levels of job satisfaction and by being more successful in everything they do. By supporting each other, mutual respect will be the outcome of these behaviours.</p>\n<p>Our Mission and Values statements provide greater detail as to &lsquo;how we work around here&rsquo;.</p>\n",
        "text": "Established by Hamish Doig in 1992, our team specialise in commercial real estate sales and leasing. Our widely experienced team have developed a reputation as being the leading provider of commercial real estate services in the South Island. We also have held the honour of being Colliers International NZ franchise of the year. History of South Island Commercial Limited Hamish Doig is Managing Director of Colliers International in Christchurch. He founded the Christchurch office of Colliers International in 1992, fully purchasing it in 1998. In 2004 the name changed to South Island Commercial (2004) Limited, trading as Colliers International, and in June 2015 it changed to South Island Commercial Limited when Mark Macauley joined the company as a shareholder and General Manager. From an original staff of 4, we have grown to 31. In September 2014 Agri Realty Limited joined the Colliers family of businesses. The Agri business works from our Christchurch office, and they also have an office in Ashburton. The shareholders of this company are Shane O'Brien, Ruth Hodges, Greg Anderson and Hamish Doig. Vision To be a highly respected professional services organisation that consistently provides quality solutions to its clients. This will be provided by a committed and motivated team of professionals who will ensure the continual development of a sustainable, quality driven business through their own continual development. Core Values Our CAN DO values are at the core of all we do: C reate a client focussed environment A ble to focus, prioritise and achieve satisfaction for clients N urture relationships with clients, listen, collaborate and provide them with efficient service D o be responsible & resilient & do as promised O pen communication, honestly and with a mind open to change, both internally and externally Organisational Culture We want a culture which supports and encourages initiative, creativity, imagination, flexibility, hard work, responsibility and the ability to spot and grasp business opportunities. We want open and honest two-way communications. Teamwork, collaboration and cooperation are rewarded through the team enjoying greater levels of job satisfaction and by being more successful in everything they do. By supporting each other, mutual respect will be the outcome of these behaviours. Our Mission and Values statements provide greater detail as to ‘how we work around here’."
