        "id": "2-1",
        "num": "2.1",
        "title": "Broker REA Licensing",
        "html": "\n<p><a href=\"https://cjch.sharepoint.com/sites/Admin/Shared%20Documents/OPERATIONS/DASHBOARDS/Real%20Estate%20Agent%20Management%20Dashboard.xlsx?web=1\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">All broker licensing expiry information (SharePoint master copy)</a> &mdash; or use the <strong>Team Dashboard &rsaquo; Roster &amp; Compliance</strong> tab on this page, which is built from the same data.</p>\n<p>At the start of each month, go to the License Expiry column and anyone due to renew their license that month is highlighted in red. Once identified, send the broker a reminder email. Brokers are responsible for renewing their own licenses &mdash; the onus is on them to remember.</p>\n<h4>Consequences for not renewing a license</h4>\n<p><strong>1. Immediate expiration and stand-down.</strong> The moment the expiry date passes without renewal and payment of the annual levies ($724.50 incl. GST), the license is automatically cancelled. The agent cannot legally carry out any real estate agency work from that date, and must immediately stand down from all listings, client interactions, marketing, and contract negotiations.</p>\n<p><strong>2. A brand-new license is required.</strong> An expired license cannot simply be reactivated by paying a late fee &mdash; an entirely new application must be submitted through the REA portal.</p>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>The process takes time:</strong> a new application typically takes 2&ndash;3 weeks to process, because it requires a mandatory public notice period to allow for objections.</li>\n<li><strong>The revenue hit:</strong> the agent is legally barred from practicing during this multi-week processing buffer, so cannot facilitate deals or collect commissions on new business during this time.</li>\n</ul>\n",
        "text": "All broker licensing expiry information (SharePoint master copy) — or use the Team Dashboard › Roster & Compliance tab on this page, which is built from the same data. At the start of each month, go to the License Expiry column and anyone due to renew their license that month is highlighted in red. Once identified, send the broker a reminder email. Brokers are responsible for renewing their own licenses — the onus is on them to remember. Consequences for not renewing a license 1. Immediate expiration and stand-down. The moment the expiry date passes without renewal and payment of the annual levies ($724.50 incl. GST), the license is automatically cancelled. The agent cannot legally carry out any real estate agency work from that date, and must immediately stand down from all listings, client interactions, marketing, and contract negotiations. 2. A brand-new license is required. An expired license cannot simply be reactivated by paying a late fee — an entirely new application must be submitted through the REA portal. The process takes time: a new application typically takes 2–3 weeks to process, because it requires a mandatory public notice period to allow for objections. The revenue hit: the agent is legally barred from practicing during this multi-week processing buffer, so cannot facilitate deals or collect commissions on new business during this time."
